-- title:
--   Reducedness of κ(A)⊗_A R versus R/(a) for principal mathfrak m_A
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring and let $a \in A$ be an element such that the maximal ideal of $A$ equals the principal ideal generated by $a$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_A = (a)$. Let $R$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $A$-algebra structure, with structure morphism $\varphi = \mathrm{algebraMap}\ A\ R$. The theorem asserts the equivalence of two reducedness statements: the $A$-algebra $\kappa(A) \otimes_A R$, where $\kappa(A) = A/\mathfrak m_A$ is the residue field of $A$, is reduced if and only if the quotient ring $R/(\varphi(a))$, by the ideal of $R$ generated by the image $\varphi(a)$ of $a$, is reduced. Here reducedness is Mathlib's `IsReduced`, i.e. the ring is nontrivial-free of nonzero nilpotents in the usual sense that every element whose some power vanishes is itself zero. No finiteness, flatness or Noetherian hypothesis is imposed on $A$ or $R$, and $a$ need not be a nonzerodivisor.
--
--   This is the standard base-change identity $(A/\mathfrak a)\otimes_A R \cong R/\mathfrak a R$ in the case of a principal maximal ideal, packaged as a transfer of the property of being reduced. It is used to pass between the two shapes in which reducedness of a special fibre appears in the study of modular curves: local charts produce a quotient of $R$ by the image of a uniformiser, while the local-to-global statements are phrased for $\kappa(A) \otimes_A R$; both citing results concern reducedness of residue-field tensor products of adic completions in the full-level modular curve package.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_isReduced_residueField_tensorProduct_iff_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span.lean

